{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792188496,"nonce":"Fyc0vtZHAFstWpHh9d8DcnJUVuA=","message":"Fixed in 6500b4029cca53e615bfe7431ca5c1be901077d0. The interpreter read a dynamic field through hlp_dyn_get* with no trap armed (its dynamic field write already ran under one), so a cast that failed inside the read called hlp_throw with nothing to catch it and aborted. The read now runs under the same setjmp boundary and the error reaches the Haxe catch. Six call sites (field get, this-field get, the virtual fallbacks and the structural closure lookup) use the new checked reader.\n\nNew test dyn_field_cast: ClosureCastRepro's shape plus a direct read and a method read, in interp, hybrid and jit, against stock HashLink's output. d017dd4 (a native HDLL calling hl_throw) is a different path and is not covered by this change.","files":null}]}